{
  "answer": "To customize or extend the generated OpenAPI schema in FastAPI, you can use the `custom_openapi()` function to generate the OpenAPI schema and then modify it as needed. This function allows you to add custom properties to the OpenAPI schema, such as a custom logo, by modifying the `info` \"object\" in the schema. For example, you can add a custom logo by setting the `x-logo` property in the `info` object. This customization can be done by modifying the OpenAPI schema directly or by using the `.openapi_schema` property to cache the schema and reuse it for subsequent requests. For more details, refer to the documentation in [how-to/extending-openapi-6] and [how-to/extending-openapi-7].",
